    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d972">

                <pb facs="1012" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.00 Revolutions/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-03T14:00:00-05:00">January 3, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Your 9, January 2, 10 p.m. In view of the overthrow of the Panaman Government
                    the Department feels that this Government cannot be called upon to allow
                    transportation of troops across the Canal Zone or to Colon via the Panama
                    Railroad as a matter of right under Article 19 of the Treaty of 1903.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d972-f1"/> The Department leaves to your discretion the
                    granting of such right of transit to the <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi>
                    authorities for purposes of pacification but you should not grant such requests
                    if to do so would lead to fighting in the Canal Zone or the cities of Panama and
                    Colon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
